;; Controls of the second test of the guard of the test tool, the check of
;; static names (see ../../../tools/flsemantics.ml, "The check of static
;; names"; decision D60): the handler of a continuation has in scope only
;; what is bound on every way to it. Each X.fl is a text written by hand;
;; the first words of its comment say what the check must do with it, MUST
;; BE REFUSED or MUST PASS, and the comment says why. README.md has the
;; table of the controls and says what they tell apart.
;;
;; run.sh runs the tool on each text alone and with the text as the term
;; after too (the option -after), and on a text that must be refused beside
;; a plain unit, as the term after and as the term before. The tool exits
;; with the status 1 where the term after is out of scope, which is why
;; these texts are not in the directory two levels up, whose rules take the
;; status 0 and no other. run.sh prints the status of each run, and fails
;; where a run is not as the comment of its text says.
;;
;; To add a control, add X.fl (its module symbol must match its name) and
;; nothing else: there is no list. `dune promote` updates scope.expected.

(rule
 (deps
  (glob_files *.fl))
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   scope.output
   (run sh %{dep:run.sh} %{dep:../../../tools/flsemantics.exe} %{deps}))))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (diff scope.expected scope.output)))
